  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `paginate.py` and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes (1 test, OK).\n\nThe bug was in how `paginate` works out where a page starts. Pages are numbered from 1, but the code started page `p` at `p * page_size`, which skipped the whole first page. For example, page 1 of `[1,2,3,4,5]` with size 2 returned `[3, 4]`. It now starts at `(page - 1) * page_size`, the same formula `page_bounds` already uses.\n\nI also checked the edges by hand. The partial last page comes back correctly (`[5]`), and a page past the end returns an empty list. I didn't touch `total_pages` or `page_bounds`.\n\nDONE: Fixed the off-by-one in paginate() by starting pages at (page - 1) * page_size instead of page * page_size; the public test passes.",
