      "elapsed_ms": 18205.919458006974,
      "final_message": "The key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nHow it gets there:\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")`.\n2. `audit.write_audit` is the only function that writes to the audit log. It builds the key as `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`.\n3. `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` in `config.py`, and `\"order\"` becomes `\"ORDER\"`, so the key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nThe key-assignment line in `audit.py` came back redacted when I printed the file, so I couldn't read it directly. I confirmed the key by calling `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")`, which returned `['AUD-ORDER-7781']`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` builds a similar-looking `MET-...` key, but it writes to a metrics dict, not the audit log.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
      "final_message_source": "stdout_response",
